29	// Import scope is exactly the document: nothing is invented, inferred or
30	// completed. A document produced by a source-scoped export rebuilds only that
31	// part of the lineage — other sources and downstreams the export omitted are
32	// not restored. Direct relations and longer branches through intermediate
33	// nodes are kept together, so explanation paths are still chosen by the
34	// existing query rules (fewest edges, then the lexicographically smallest full
35	// path in Go string order).
